asize preparation and planning over  split-second reactions that is they  change how you compose your loadout  Delta squad's skiff can store two  additional weapons meaning you can  create a moving armoury fit for an array  of situations you can prepare for what  you think is going to be a long range  shootout only to find that it is in  act a close-quarters nightmare gears  creative Arsenal's have long been a  staple of the series and the open world  subtly change how you outfit your  characters well you could make the  argument that the Coalition is chasing  trends by adding open spaces to its  linear formula it does enough to make  them feel distinct it used them to  encourage planning and characterization  doing away with the fire fight cutscene  fire fight formula its relied on for so  long  although the coalition runs the risk of  alienating many fans with these  sandboxes it's refreshing to see them  reexamining what makes this series tick  as I mentioned earlier there are changes  on a smaller scale as well  tons of them and while they seem subtle  in isolation they all combine to create  a much different combat flow than I've  experienced in Gears fives predecessors  these range from basic stealth to a  deeper melee system Gears 5 also does  away with the reticle bloom of earlier  installments opting instead for actual  weapon recoil in essence they've changed  how it feels to play a Gears game  traditional wisdom says not to fix what  isn't broken but this is the rare  exception what's more Gears 5 implements  a companion character that rivaled the  likes of at Reyes in God of War by  upgrading your squad's robot aka the  ever loveable Jack he allows you to  cloak around enemies opening them to  brutal finishing attacks he can freeze  opponents where they stand shortly  before your squad shatters them from  cover he can even fetch you ammo items  and weapons and trust me when I say that  this ability is his most useful by far  the result of these minor tweaks is that  I'm actually spending more time out of  cover than ever before considering Gears  defined the cover based shooter and  built a legacy on it to boot it's  strange to be out in the open sending a  robot to stun someone while I sprint up  with a cloak on and execute them from  behind even on harder difficulties Gears  5 encourages me to be creative with my  approach and it's rewarding every step  of the way  there are numerous other changes the  Coalition has introduced to its namesake  franchise but all of this is to say that  despite how divisive some of them will  undoubtedly be it's promising to see a  studio attempting to change things the  Coalition will always be wrestling with  the past in one way or another Gears of  War 4 is safe approach is  proof of that but it feels like the  studio has finally hit its stride gears  5 feels like the developer had an  absolute blast  making it and for me that fun is  infectious I can only hope the coalition  continues to be so bold  you
 

